          "thinking": "All tests pass. Now I need to implement the changes. Let me understand what needs to be done:\n\n1. Add `entries_b64` to the allowed fields for orphan bodies in `check_body`\n2. Create the `_orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None` function\n3. Wire it into wherever orphans are checked - primarily in `cmd_monitor` where orphans are processed\n\nLet me look at the monitor command more carefully to understand where to wire in the check.\n\nIn `cmd_monitor`, orphans are processed here:\n```python\nexplained = {e[\"body\"][\"log_index\"]: e for e, _ in chain if e[\"kind\"] == \"orphan\"}\n...\nif idx in explained:\n    o = explained[idx]\n    body = json.loads(base64.b64decode(v[\"body\"]))\n    stmt = base64.b64decode(o[\"body\"][\"statement_b64\"])\n    if body.get(\"kind\") != \"dsse\" or body[\"spec\"][\"payloadHash\"][\"value\"] != hashlib.sha256(stmt).hexdigest():\n        bad.append(f\"orphan entry {o['seq']}: its statement isn't the one Rekor holds for log index {idx}\")\n        continue\n    pred = (parse_json(stmt, f\"orphan entry {o['seq']} statement\") or {}).get(\"predicate\") or {}\n    head = pred.get(\"head_sha256\")\n    if head in published and head not in current:\n        bad.append(f\"orphan entry {o['seq']}: the attested head {head} was published on {a.git_rev} and later removed\")\n        continue\n    orphans.append(dict(row, explained_by_entry=o[\"seq\"], attested_range=f\"{pred.get('from_seq')}-{pred.get('to_seq')}\"))\n```\n\nThis is where I should add the check for `_orphan_entries_problem`. The `pred` variable contains the predicate with `from_seq`, `to_seq`, `prev_sha256`, `head_sha256`.\n\nAlso, I should add validation in `check_body` for orphans to allow `entries_b64` field.\n\nLet me implement this.",
