          "type": "thinking",
          "thinking": "The implementation is complete. Let me summarize what was done:\n\n1. Added `entries_b64` to the allowed fields for orphan bodies in `check_body()` with validation that each entry is a valid base64 string.\n\n2. Created the `_orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None` function that:\n   - Returns `None` when the decoded entries exactly match the attested range\n   - Returns a string containing \"range\" when the count is wrong or sequence numbers don't match\n   - Returns a string containing \"chain\" when an entry's `prev` doesn't link correctly\n   - Returns a string containing \"head\" when the last entry's hash doesn't match `head_sha256`\n\n3. Wired the function into `cmd_monitor` where orphans are checked against Rekor attestations.\n\n4. All existing tests pass.",
          "signature": ""
