        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of the changes made to `/workspace/record/record.py`:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. Added `entries_b64` to orphan body schema (in `check_body`)\n- Added `\"entries_b64\"` to the allowed fields for orphan entries\n- Added validation that `entries_b64` is a list of valid base64 strings\n\n### 2. Created `_orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None` function\nThe function validates that an orphan's `entries_b64` matches the attested range in the predicate:\n- **Returns `None`** when valid: correct count, proper chain linking from `prev_sha256`, correct sequence numbers, and final hash matches `head_sha256`\n- **Returns problem string containing:**\n  - `\"range\"` when entry count is wrong or sequence numbers don't match expected range\n  - `\"chain\"` when an entry's `prev` field doesn't link to the previous entry's hash\n  - `\"head\"` when the last entry's hash doesn't match `pred[\"head_sha256\"]`\n\n### 3. Wired into `cmd_monitor`\nAdded the validation check in the monitor command where orphans are verified against Rekor attestations. If an orphan's `entries_b64` doesn't match the attested predicate, it's reported as a problem in the `bad` list.\n\n### 4. All existing tests pass\nThe 19 existing tests in `test_record.py` continue to pass, confirming backward compatibility."
